WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Drag equation. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Identify density, area, Cd and speed

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: The drag model D = ½ρCdAv² organizes density, coefficient, reference area and speed. Cd and area must use compatible conventions.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: With ρ=1.225 kg/m³, Cd=.32, A=2.2 m² and v=25 m/s, the illustrative fixed-input model gives about 270 N.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Variable matching

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Identify density, area, Cd and speed
